  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 104.37 “Process” means either of the following depending on the purpose for its use:\n\n(a) For purposes of RSA 125-C, “process” means any operation that combines devices, equipment, raw materials, utilities, and manpower for the production of goods, services, energy, pollution control, or other purposes; or\n\n(b) For purposes of RSA 125-I, “process” means “process” as defined in RSA 125-I:2, XII, reprinted in Appendix C.\n\nSource. #1717, eff 2-19-81; ss by #2332, eff 4-29-83; ss by #2938, eff 12-27-84; ss by #5033, eff 12-27-90; ss and moved by #6057-A, eff 6-30-95 (from Env-A 101.73); ss by #6328, INTERIM, eff 8-24-96, EXPIRED: 12-22-96\n\nNew. #6468-A, eff 3-5-97; renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.214), (see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading); renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.148), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.150) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
